00:05:09,473 --> 00:05:15,473
In 2019, the most precious natural resource... is us.

2
00:10:18,947 --> 00:10:24,947
Daybreakers is a action, fantasy, science fiction
film directed by Michael Spierig.

3
00:15:28,421 --> 00:15:34,421
In the year 2019, a plague has transformed almost every human into a vampire.

4
00:20:37,894 --> 00:20:43,894
Faced with a dwindling blood supply, the fractured dominant race plots their survival;
meanwhile, a researcher works with a covert band of vampires on a way to save humankind.

5
00:25:47,368 --> 00:25:53,368
Edward Dalton, played by Ethan Hawke.

6
00:30:56,842 --> 00:31:02,842
Charles Bromley, played by Sam Neill.

7
00:36:06,315 --> 00:36:12,315
Lionel 'Elvis' Cormac, played by Willem Dafoe.

8
00:41:15,789 --> 00:41:21,789
Audrey Bennett, played by Claudia Karvan.

9
00:46:25,263 --> 00:46:31,263
Alison Bromley, played by Isabel Lucas.

10
00:51:34,736 --> 00:51:40,736
Christopher Caruso, played by Vince Colosimo.

11
00:56:44,210 --> 00:56:50,210
Daybreakers is a 2009 dystopian sci-fi action-horror vampire film
written and directed by Michael and Peter Spierig.

12
01:01:53,684 --> 01:01:59,684
The film takes place in a futuristic world overrun by vampires, and centers around a vampiric corporation which
sets out to capture and farm the remaining humans while researching a substitute for human blood.

13
01:07:03,157 --> 01:07:09,157
Ethan Hawke plays vampire hematologist Edward Dalton, whose work is interrupted by human survivors led by
former vampire 'Elvis' (Willem Dafoe), who has a cure that can save the human species.

14
01:12:12,631 --> 01:12:18,631
An international co-production between the United States and Australia,
Daybreakers premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival in 2009.

15
01:17:22,105 --> 01:17:28,105
It was released in the United Kingdom on 6 January 2010
and in North America on 8 January 2010.

16
01:22:31,578 --> 01:22:37,578
The film grossed over $50 million worldwide (from a $20 million
budget) and received mixed-to-positive critical reception.

17
01:27:41,052 --> 01:27:47,052
The film explores themes of experiment, sunrise, waitress, vampire, dystopia.

18
01:32:50,526 --> 01:32:56,526
The tone is uplifting and dark and thought_provoking.
